{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421640-netflix-\u2018blood-of-zeus\u2019-as-scion-chronicle","id":1421640,"title":"Netflix \u2018Blood of Zeus\u2019 as Scion chronicle","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-11-03T09:46:08-08:00","id":1421640,"title":"Netflix \u2018Blood of Zeus\u2019 as Scion chronicle","content":"I started to watch Netflix animation series \u2018<b>Blood of Zeus</b>\u2019 ( <b>BoZ </b>in short ), similar to <i>Castlevania</i>, but this time based on Greek Mythology. Plot is centered on next child of Zeus. It\u2019s generally looks like screenwriters made new myth. And it\u2019s cool.<br /> <br /> The best part for <b>Scion</b> are monsters. Graphics of monsters and gods are really good here. ( Even if general animation has lacks of low budget now. ) Most important are images of Titans, Giants and demons in <b>BoZ</b>.<br /> <br /> From <b>Scion</b> point of view, <b>BoZ</b> Titan shown as Primordial of Darkness? Then <b>BoZ </b>Giants looks more like proper Theoi Titans of <b>Scion</b>? And then, so called \u2018demons\u2019 are variant of titanspawn in <b>BoZ</b> setting? Do I get it right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T09:52:26-08:00","id":1421641,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>BoZ Titan</b></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" o